{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/966190-veritas","id":966190,"title":"Veritas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-09T07:02:17-07:00","id":966190,"title":"Veritas","content":"I feel there's something wrong with the Veritas Alembic's Persistent effect.<br /> <br /> <b>p.160:</b> &quot;Any supernatural power that garners a number of successes equal to or greater than the Promethean\u2019s Azoth used within (Azoth x 5) yards of the character alerts the Promethean.&quot;<br /> <br /> This mechanic seems to imply that the weaker a character's Azoth is, the easier it is to detect other supernaturals' powers. This makes no sense to me. Powers should be easier to detect with a stronger Azoth.<br /> <br /> Is this correct, or am I misinterpreting it? Developer attention to this would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5766-nouveaurich","name":"NouveauRich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5766_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:37:00-07:00","id":966206,"title":"","content":"I was confused at first, but I think it's a way to filter out weak powers so that you encounter stronger supers to study or fight.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that you can dampen your Azoth, so if you really want to find weaker powers, you still can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><s